<section class="text-level-4">
  <h2>Several ways to run tests</h2>

  <ul class="mt--50">
    <li class="fragment">
      Headless (no browser window will be opened)
      <pre class="mt-50r"><code class="sh">
                npx playwright test
            </code></pre>

      <ul class="mt-75r">
        <li>Best for continous integration</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="fs-60p">
        More info:
        <span>https://playwright.dev/docs/test-cli</span>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="mt-150r fragment">
      With UI
      <pre class="mt-50r"><code class="sh">
        npx playwright test --ui
      </code></pre>

      <ul class="mt-75r">
        <li>To run test suites on your local machine</li>
        <li>
          To inspect what happened before, during, and after each step of your
          tests
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="fs-60p">
        More info:
        <span>https://playwright.dev/docs/test-ui-mode</span>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="mt-150r fragment">
      With VS Code
      <ul class="mt-25r">
        <li>The most convenient to implement and debug tests</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="fs-60p">
        More info:
        <span>https://playwright.dev/docs/getting-started-vscode</span>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="mt-150r fragment">
      Headed with CLI
      <pre class="mt-50r"><code class="sh">
        npx playwright test --headed --debug tests/some-feature.test.ts:6
        # --headed opens a browser with a UI
        # --debug keeps the browser open at the end of the test
      </code></pre>
      <ul class="mt-25r">
        <li>To use when you don't have VScode...</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="fs-60p">
        More info:
        <span>https://playwright.dev/docs/getting-started-vscode</span>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
